# Larn Module license

Covers `external/larn/`, `src/modules/larn/native/`, and the built
`public/modules/larn/*`.

## 1. Governing license — Noah Morgan's grant (1986)

Larn shipped with no license file. Morgan stated his terms in a Usenet
post a month before the release of Larn 12.0, "larn and coming attractions"
(`net.sources.games`, 10 July 1986):

> Larn was distributed to the net for the enjoyment of all. One of my goals
> is to have larn available to whom ever wants to play it. I therefore give
> permission to use the sources, to modify the sources, or to port the
> sources to another machine, provided that a profit is not made from larn
> or its sources, or the aforementioned activities. Should a profit be made
> without permissions, I will exercise my copyright. Other than this case,
> enjoy it!

**Provenance.** The post is archived at
<https://groups.google.com/g/net.sources.games/c/G7Dr8fodSYk/m/-lzwfiEmrMEJ>;
the grant follows "I'd also like to clarify my position on the source code to
larn:" and is quoted above word for word (checked against the archive
2026-11-02). A copy of the whole post is kept in
`docs/licensing/1986-07-10-morgan-larn-and-coming-attractions.txt`. Secondary sources that date it August 1986 are thinking of the
`larn 12.0` source posting (8 August 1986,
<https://groups.google.com/g/net.sources.games/c/NFjRJz2NcFU>), which carries
only the per-file "Larn is copyrighted 1986 by Noah Morgan" headers and no
grant.

`external/larn/COPYRIGHT` records Morgan's copyright over the vendored tree
("This entire subtree is copyright by Noah Morgan"); it does not itself
contain the grant. "Profit" is undefined in the grant, and the wording
predates browser delivery — see LICENSING.md for the project's reliance
position.

## 2. Notices carried within — BSD-licensed files

Six NetBSD-era files in `external/larn/` carry their own permissive notices.
Clause 2 of each requires the notice to accompany binary distributions, and
`larn.wasm` compiles these files, so both notices are reproduced below.

These files remain under their own BSD grants — Morgan's permission is not
copyleft and does not re-license them. Their conditions (attribution, notice
reproduction, and the UCB non-endorsement clause) apply **in addition to**
Morgan's no-profit condition, which is what binds redistribution of the
Module as a whole. `src/modules/larn/native/`, being VectHack's own work,
stays MIT.

### University of California, 3-clause

Applies to five files, whose Regents copyright lines differ by year:

- `data.c`, `store.c` — Copyright (c) 1988 The Regents of the University of
  California. All rights reserved.
- `pathnames.h` — Copyright (c) 1990 The Regents of the University of
  California. All rights reserved.
- `bill.c`, `fortune.c` — Copyright (c) 1991 The Regents of the University of
  California. All rights reserved.

The conditions and disclaimer are identical in all five; reproduced here from
`bill.c`, whose 1991 line stands for the notice body:

